# Path rules for agent edits, read by guard-path.sh and turned into OpenCode's
# permission.edit block by gen-opencode-rules.sh.
#
# Format: <deny|ask> <glob> <way forward shown to the agent>
# Globs are repo-relative and * crosses /, matching OpenCode's wildcard.
#
# deny: generator output. Edit the generator's input instead.
# ask:  files an agent may edit but could use to weaken its own guardrails.

deny internal/adapters/sqlite/sqlcgen/* edit db/queries/*.sql or db/migrations/*.sql and run `make generate-sql`
deny internal/domain/value/languages_gen.go run `make generate-languages`
deny mocks_test.go edit .mockery.yml and run `make generate-mocks`
deny */mocks_test.go edit .mockery.yml and run `make generate-mocks`
deny *_enum.go edit the enum declaration and run `make generate-enums`
deny go.sum run `go mod tidy`
deny opencode.json edit scripts/agent/protected-paths and run `make generate-agent-rules`

ask scripts/agent/* this file guards the agent hooks; the user must approve the edit
ask .claude/settings.json this file wires the agent hooks; the user must approve the edit
ask .opencode/* this file wires the agent hooks; the user must approve the edit
ask .agents/hooks.json this file wires the agent hooks; the user must approve the edit
ask lefthook.yml this file configures the git hooks; the user must approve the edit
ask .golangci.yml this file configures the linters; the user must approve the edit
ask .go-arch-lint.yml this file configures the layer rules; the user must approve the edit
ask .github/workflows/* this file configures CI; the user must approve the edit
ask mise.toml this file pins the toolchain; the user must approve the edit
